<span style="color:Yellow">You both imagine the explosion that follows, sending you both flying back against the wall as the mind control rays scatter out.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>, far enough away, isn’t hit much. <span style="color:Yellow">But due to you holding it, your mind is altered and warped.</span> Or, at least, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> explains that it is in the make-believe adventure you two are going on. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh no, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>! Are you-!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Yellow">starts to ask when you suddenly blast him with your power, sending him flying back into his beanbag!</span> You laugh evilly, proclaiming that you are now a villain and he’ll have to defeat you if he ever hopes to get his friend and ally back! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh no! But how can I fight my friend? What a cruel twist of fate!”</span> <span style="color:LightGreen">Despite trying to act devastated and worried, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> can’t hide his smile as the two of you begin an epic, pretend battle that will shake the very foundations of the world! Or, at least, in your minds they do.</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Battle Carter">>
    You and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> use your powers against each other, you attacking from a range with your powers as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> rushes and dodges to try and get in close to deliver a devastating smash against you! You manage to just barely duck under one, sending <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s fist into the wall and shaking the entire building so much you fear the roof may collapse! <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">$CarterNickname</span>! You can fight this! You have to!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> pleads, not wanting to hurt his friend, but you simply scoff at his feeble attempts to bring you back. You live on the side of evil now! <br>

