    You laugh as you hold the shirt up, saying that without it he is powerless! <span style="color:Pink">That is, of course, unless his bottoms are also a source of his power.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I mean, sometimes…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> says, out of character, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But that’d be weird to do, haha. So, let’s just say it’s the shirt. So, without it, I’m powerless!”</span> He explains, realizing that he dodged a bullet by you going to his shirt first. You hear him mumble to himself that he really should have just said his shirt only to begin with. <br>
    <br>
    The battle resumes while he is still mumbling, you push <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> onto the bed as you kick something out from under it, having spotted the box and remembered what it held. <span style="color:Pink">You quickly bend down and grab the handcuffs, the jingle of the metal alerting <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to what you have. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“W- wait! I don’t think we should use those until we-!”</span> But you don’t listen, using one hand to force <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span>’s hands to his bedpost as you slip on the handcuffs in one swift motion, never feeling so cool in your life. They click, completely and securely, not at all like the pretend click <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> tried to do.</span> <br>

