    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“W- what just happened!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> <span style="color:Pink">yanks at the cuffs, a nervous smile and worried eyes filling his flushed face. They don’t budge and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> gulps as he realizes the situation he is suddenly in. He is handcuffed to his bed, hands stuck above his head. In an instant he is suddenly completely at the mercy of his mind-controlled friend and ally. You smile down at him, asking the hero what he plans to do now.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I… uhh…”</span> He yanks at them a few more times, hoping that they didn’t actually lock. He gives you a smile, obviously a little nervous to be actually bound and cuffed to his bed, but still continues to play along, enjoying just how real the game is feeling. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“D- do your worst, villain! I still believe my friend is in there and he’ll break free from this mind control any minute!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You give your best evil laugh, one that actually causes <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Carter</span> to jump a little. You tell the little hero that he is going to give you all the hero secrets he has in his brain, or else. <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Or- or else?”</span> He gives you a look that is equal parts nervous, fear, and excitement. The boy truly has no idea what he’s in for.</span> <br>
    <br>

